window.__FALLBACK_GLOSSARY__ = {"updatedAt":"2026-11-23T07:40:00+09:00","title":"Terms & product notes","intro":"In addition to petrochemical and plastic raw materials, the processes, specifications, yields, and transaction units of steel, non-ferrous metals, agricultural products, food raw materials, energy, batteries, and precious metals were confirmed and organized using public primary data (World Steel Association, LME, USGS, USDA, FAO, MPOB, ICO, ICE, Korean Standards Association, etc.). Past price examples include the timing, and the current standard value can be checked in the market situation table above.","notice":"The properties listed here are representative public data sheet values. The actual value varies depending on the grade, test standard, and molding conditions, so it must be confirmed with the supplier's TDS (technical data) before ordering. This page is not a basis for trading or investment decisions, but is a reference for understanding terms.","categories":[{"id":"oil","label":"Crude oil and refining"},{"id":"feed","label":"Basic oil and intermediate materials"},{"id":"resin","label":"Synthetic resins"},{"id":"comp","label":"Reinforcements and additives"},{"id":"trade","label":"Market price and trading practice"},{"id":"app","label":"Product/Application"},{"id":"steel","label":"Steel and non-ferrous metals"},{"id":"agri","label":"Agricultural products and raw materials"},{"id":"energy","label":"Energy·Battery·Other"}],"entries":[{"id":"crude","term":"Crude Oil","ko":"Crude oil and fractional distillation","cat":"oil","summary":"Crude oil is divided by boiling point difference to extract fuel and petrochemical raw materials (naphtha). It is the starting point of the petrochemical tree.","facts":[["Proportion going to raw materials","Most of the crude oil is used as fuel for transportation, heating, and power generation, and only about 10% goes to petrochemical raw materials such as plastics."],["Product yield of domestic oil refineries (2023)","Diesel 28.3%, Naphtha 24.6%, Gasoline 13.9%, Jet fuel 11.2%, Heavy oil 6.2%, LPG 2.2% (Korea Petroleum Association)"],["Separation Principle","In an atmospheric distillation column, it is divided from top (light fraction) to bottom (heavy fraction) due to differences in boiling point depending on the number of carbons and bonding structure."]],"body":["Crude oil is a liquid containing a small amount of impurities mixed with hydrocarbons where carbon and hydrogen are combined. When heated and placed in an atmospheric distillation tower, components with low boiling points are extracted from the top and components with high boiling points are extracted from the bottom and split into LPG, gasoline, naphtha, kerosene, diesel oil, heavy oil, and asphalt.","Among these, naphtha, which corresponds to heavy gasoline, is the main raw material for petrochemicals. When naphtha is thermally decomposed in a naphtha cracking facility (NCC), ethylene, propylene, C4, and BTX are produced, and the schematic diagram on this page leads to the products below.","Oil refineries don’t stop there. Because we run an upgrading facility that converts the heavy oil remaining under the tower back into light oil through reduced pressure distillation, catalytic cracking, and hydrocracking, the actual product composition is greatly different from the simple distillation yield."],"caution":"The widely cited values ​​of 2% LPG, 8% gasoline, 12% naphtha, 9% kerosene, 26% diesel oil, 38% heavy oil, and 5% other are conceptual approximate values ​​for when crude oil is once atmospherically distilled. The actual yield (table above) of domestic oil refineries reduces heavy oil by 6% and increases the proportion of diesel and naphtha thanks to advanced facilities.","sources":[{"name":"Korea Petroleum Association, Current Status of Domestic Petroleum Industry (December 2024)","url":"https://www.pcccr.go.kr/storage/board/base/2024/12/11/BOARD_ATTACH_1733883271139.pdf"},{"name":"GS Caltex Media Hub, atmospheric residual oil and upgrading process","url":"https://gscaltexmediahub.com/energy/energy-encyclopedia/video-ar-cracker-201912/"}]},{"id":"benchmark","term":"WTI / Brent / Dubai","ko":"Three major reference oils for international oil prices","cat":"oil","summary":"The value of the same crude oil varies depending on the region in which it is announced. You must first check what the ‘price’ of the news is.","facts":[["WTI","Made in West Texas, USA, light low sulfur. Based on New York Mercantile Exchange (NYMEX) futures."],["Brent","Based on the North Sea. London ICE futures are the most cited indicator of international oil prices."],["Dubai","Based on Middle Eastern products. It is used as a standard price for Asian crude oil imports."]],"body":["Price differences for the three standard oils are usually maintained due to differences in crude oil quality (specific gravity and sulfur content) and supply regions. Generally, Dubai is the lowest and Brent is the highest, but when the situation in the Middle East shakes, the order is sometimes reversed with Dubai gaining a premium.","The data compiled from the Price Association Notice in January 2024 states that ‘Dubai is not cheap now.’ This is a phenomenon that reflects the Middle East risks at the time, and is not an absolute rule."],"caution":"This information describes the notice table as of writing on 2024-01-24. Please check the oil price section of the market table above for the current three standard oil prices and spreads.","sources":[{"name":"Market status table on this page — Oil price/exchange rate (international crude oil standard)","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#market-quotes"}]},{"id":"naphtha","term":"Naphtha","ko":"Naphtha","cat":"oil","summary":"Heavy gasoline fraction from crude oil distillation. It is virtually the only starting raw material for domestic petrochemicals.","facts":[["Domestic production yield","In 2023, 24.6% of domestic oil refinery products were naphtha (Korea Petroleum Association)."],["Main use","Naphtha cracking facility (NCC) input → ethylene·propylene, reforming facility → BTX."],["Pricing Structure","Naphtha prices account for a large portion of NCC costs, and the naphtha-ethylene spread is used as a barometer of the petrochemical industry."]],"body":["When crude oil is distilled, it comes out in the order from lightest to LPG, gasoline, naphtha, kerosene, diesel, and heavy oil. Among these, naphtha is an oil with a carbon number of approximately 5 to 11. It is also used as fuel, but in Korea, it is mostly used as a petrochemical raw material.","Naphtha is pyrolyzed in NCC with steam at 800~900℃ to produce ethylene and propylene, and at the same time, C4 oil and pyrolysis gasoline (Pygas) are produced as by-products. The BTX system extracts benzene, toluene, and xylene from Pygas."],"sources":[{"name":"Korea Petroleum Association, Current Status of Domestic Petroleum Industry (December 2024)","url":"https://www.pcccr.go.kr/storage/board/base/2024/12/11/BOARD_ATTACH_1733883271139.pdf"},{"name":"S-OIL, information on oil refining process","url":"https://www.s-oil.com/m/energy/Process.aspx"}]},{"id":"olefins","term":"Ethylene / Propylene","ko":"Ethylene/Propylene","cat":"feed","summary":"The two most basic basic fractions obtained by decomposing naphtha. Almost all synthetic resins split here.","facts":[["ethylene","Raw materials for PE, PVC (via EDC), EG, SM (via ethylbenzene). Domestic facility capacity 13,012 thousand tons/year (June 2025)."],["propylene","Raw materials for PP, AN, PO, acrylic acid, and cumene (phenol). Domestic facility capacity: 11,165,000 tons/year (June 2025)."],["Unit sense","1 ton of PP contains 1.05 to 1.10 tons of propylene, and 1 ton of HDPE contains 1.02 to 1.04 tons of ethylene (unit table on this page)."]],"body":["Ethylene and propylene are gases at room temperature, so it is difficult to sell them as is, and most of them are sent directly to the next process through pipes in the same complex. So, the prices of these two items are discussed as a spread between the ‘raw material naphtha value’ and the ‘next process product price’.","Ethylene leads to PE·PVC·EG, propylene to PP·AN·PO, and by-product C4 goes through butadiene to become a rubber component of synthetic rubber (BR·SBR·NBR) and ABS. Cracker operations and product distribution change depending on which product is profitable."],"sources":[{"name":"This page’s petrochemical schematic (2025.6, 1,000MTA)","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#petchem"},{"name":"Unit Consumption Table on this page","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"}]},{"id":"btx","term":"BTX / PX","ko":"Benzene, toluene, xylene and paraxylene","cat":"feed","summary":"Framework of the aromatic family. Benzene leads to SM, phenol, and caprolactam, and paraxylene leads to TPA and DMT.","facts":[["Benzene (BZ)","Raw materials for SM, phenol, cyclohexane (caprolactam), and aniline (MDI). Domestic facility capacity: 7,772,000 tons/year."],["Paraxylene (PX)","Raw materials for TPA·DMT. With a domestic facility capacity of 10,790,000 tons/year, it is the center of domestic aromatics."],["Production Path","It is extracted from naphtha reforming (RFCC, Reformer) and pyrolysis gasoline (Pygas), and the yield of benzene and PX is adjusted by converting toluene and xylene."]],"body":["BTX is an acronym for benzene, toluene, and xylene. The three substances can be converted to each other (toluene disproportionation, hydrogen dealkylation, etc.), increasing production of specific items by changing facility operation according to market prices.","When only para-xylene is separated from the xylene mixture and oxidized, it becomes TPA, and when esterified with methanol, it becomes DMT. This is why the cost of polyester (PET) and engineering plastics (PBT) is ultimately tied to the PX value."],"sources":[{"name":"This page petrochemical schematic — BTX Plant","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#petchem"},{"name":"Clariant explains PTA purification process","url":"https://www.clariant.com/en/Business-Units/Catalysts/Petrochemical-and-Refining-Catalysts/Ethylene-Dichloride-and-Terephthalic-Acid-Catalysts"}]},{"id":"sm","term":"Styrene Monomer (SM)","ko":"Styrene monomer","cat":"feed","summary":"Liquid monomer derived from benzene and ethylene. It is a common raw material for PS, ABS, SAN, and SBR, and is an item with large price fluctuations.","facts":[["Production Path","Benzene + ethylene → ethylbenzene → dehydrogenation (or oxidation) → SM."],["Unit consumption","1 ton of SM contains 1.10 to 1.20 tons of ethylbenzene (dehydrogenation method)."],["Used","0.93 to 1.05 tons of SM per ton of PS (GP/HI/EPS), 0.54 tons of SM per ton of ABS, and 0.70 tons of SM per ton of SAN."]],"body":["SM is one of the few basic oils that is liquid at room temperature, so it is relatively easy to store and transport, and spot trading and price announcements are active. The prices of raw materials benzene and ethylene, as well as demand for PS and ABS, determine the price.","Past market data states that ‘SM is the raw material with the largest price fluctuation among petrochemical trading items.’ In fact, SM responds sensitively to benzene prices and seasonal demand (peak season for home appliances and building materials), so it is often used as a leading indicator for predicting PS and ABS prices."],"sources":[{"name":"Basic unit table on this page — SM·PS·ABS·SAN","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"},{"name":"Market status table on this page — SM (styrene monomer)","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#market-quotes"}]},{"id":"bpa","term":"Bisphenol-A (BPA)","ko":"Bisphenol A","cat":"feed","summary":"An intermediate material made by condensing phenol and acetone. It is a common raw material for polycarbonate and epoxy resin.","facts":[["synthesis","2 molecules of phenol + 1 molecule of acetone → BPA (by-product is water). Acid-catalyzed condensation."],["Demand Structure","65-70% of the world's BPA goes to polycarbonate, and 25-30% goes to epoxy and vinyl ester resin."],["Unit consumption","1 ton of BPA, 0.88 tons of phenol, 0.28 tons of acetone (unit table on this page)."]],"body":["BPA is made by reacting phenol and acetone. The raw materials, phenol and acetone, are produced in large quantities through petrochemicals, but there are relatively few companies that can produce BPA because it requires high-purity crystallization technology.","BPA values ​​fluctuate between raw materials (phenol, acetone) and end users (PC, epoxy). BPA rose in 2021 due to a surge in demand for epoxy for wind power blades, a phenomenon that coincided with the Chinese wind power installation boom at the time.","In addition to epoxy resin, PC and flame retardants (TBBPA series) also use BPA, so PC operation rate and epoxy demand must be viewed together."],"caution":"As of 2021-03-16, the information that ‘domestically produced by Kumho P&B, LG Chemical, and Samyang Corporation’ is based on the time of writing. Current production company and facility capabilities may change, so please check with the latest data.","sources":[{"name":"Wikipedia, Bisphenol A (Uses/Production)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bisphenol_A"},{"name":"S&P Global, BPA Fair Economy Review (2020-11)","url":"https://www.spglobal.com/content/dam/spglobal/ci/en/documents/products/1025/RW2020-11_toc.pdf"},{"name":"S&P Global, Phenol CEH(2025)","url":"https://www.spglobal.com/content/dam/spglobal/ci/en/documents/products/pdf/CI_0325_Global_CEH_Phenol_Abstract.pdf"}]},{"id":"tpa-dmt","term":"TPA / DMT","ko":"Terephthalic acid, dimethyl terephthalate","cat":"feed","summary":"Polyester raw material derived from paraxylene. As TPA became mainstream, DMT facilities decreased.","facts":[["TPA","It is made by oxidizing and purifying paraxylene. Main raw material for PET·PBT."],["DMT","A form in which TPA is esterified with methanol. It was a raw material for the early PBT/PET process."],["Unit consumption","For 1 ton of PET, 0.868 to 0.88 tons of TPA + 0.327 to 0.339 tons of EG (or 1.02 to 1.066 tons of DMT + EG)."]],"body":["When para-xylene is oxidized with air, crude terephthalic acid is released, and when the remaining impurities (4-CBA) are removed by hydrogenation, it becomes purified terephthalic acid (PTA). PTA purity directly affects the color and physical properties of polyester.","DMT is a form of the same raw material reacted with methanol. In the past, it was difficult to produce high purity TPA, so the DMT diesel process (transesterification) was used, but as TPA refining technology has developed since the 1960s, most new facilities are built using the TPA direct process."],"caution":"The 2021 data states that ‘domestic TPA is being exported due to oversupply.’ This was the situation at the time, and the supply structure in Asia continues to change due to the expansion of China's PX and PTA.","sources":[{"name":"Clariant, PTA oxidation and purification catalyst","url":"https://www.clariant.com/en/Business-Units/Catalysts/Petrochemical-and-Refining-Catalysts/Ethylene-Dichloride-and-Terephthalic-Acid-Catalysts"},{"name":"European Polymer Journal, Poly(alkylene terephthalate)s review (2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eurpolymj.2021.110840"}]},{"id":"bdo","term":"1,4-Butanediol (BDO)","ko":"1,4-butanediol","cat":"feed","summary":"Raw materials for PBT, polyurethane, and PTMEG (spandex). It accounts for a larger portion of PBT costs than TPA.","facts":[["Production Path","Butadiene series, acetylene + formaldehyde (Reppe method), propylene oxide series, etc."],["Unit consumption","0.46 tons of BDO per 1 ton of PBT (based on past data). The unit unit table on this page shows 1,4-butadiene 0.44 + DMT 0.89."],["Demand","Most of them are PBT, PTMEG (spandex), and polyurethane (PU) series."]],"body":["PBT is made by condensation polymerization of BDO and TPA (or DMT). Although TPA contains a larger amount of raw materials, BDO has a much greater cost contribution. This is because the BDO manufacturing process is long and energy-consuming.","BDO has a route from butadiene and a route from acetylene. China has rapidly increased its PBT and PTMEG production capacity by establishing a large-scale coal-based acetylene → BDO route, which has exerted downward pressure on Asian PBT prices."],"caution":"The 2021-04-08 data stated that BDO rose and TPA was stable due to the spandex boom at the time. BDO supply and demand is greatly dependent on the Chinese spandex/PBAT (biodegradable resin) operation rate, so separate confirmation is required at this time.","sources":[{"name":"European Polymer Journal, PBT synthesis and BDO route (2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eurpolymj.2021.110840"},{"name":"Table of basic units on this page — PBT","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"}]},{"id":"caprolactam","term":"Caprolactam","ko":"caprolactam","cat":"feed","summary":"Monomer of nylon 6 (PA6). Benzene → Cyclohexane → Caprolactam → PA6.","facts":[["path","Benzene → Cyclohexane → Cyclohexanone/oxime → Caprolactam → Ring-opening polymerization → PA6."],["Unit consumption","1 ton of PA6 chips, 1.03 tons of caprolactam, and 1.28 tons of cyclohexane."],["Contrast","PA66 is not made from caprolactam but from HMDA (hexamethylenediamine) + adipic acid."]],"body":["Caprolactam is a ring-shaped molecule, so when heat is applied, the ring opens, allowing ring-opening polymerization to form a chain. Thanks to this, PA6 has a simpler process than PA66 and is used in both textiles and engineering plastics.","The difference between PA6 and PA66 lies in the raw materials. PA6 is a condensation polymerization of one monomer (caprolactam), and PA66 is a condensation polymerization of two monomers (HMDA + adipic acid). This difference leads to differences in melting point, strength, and hygroscopicity."],"sources":[{"name":"Intensity unit table on this page — Nylon 6/66 chips","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"},{"name":"This page petrochemical tree — Benzene → Caprolactam → PA","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#petchem"}]},{"id":"pe","term":"PE (HDPE / LDPE / LLDPE)","ko":"polyethylene","cat":"resin","summary":"The most widely used general-purpose resin. Depending on density and branch structure, it is divided into HDPE, LDPE, and LLDPE.","facts":[["Density","LDPE 0.91~0.94, HDPE 0.94~0.97 g/cm³."],["Melting point","LDPE 110~130℃, HDPE 130~135℃."],["Unit consumption","1.02 to 1.04 tons of ethylene per ton of HDPE and 1.00 to 1.05 tons of LDPE/L-LDPE."]],"body":["PE is a resin polymerized only with ethylene. Depending on the polymerization method and comonomer, the amount of branches attached to the chain varies; the fewer branches, the higher the density and stiffness.","HDPE is used where rigidity is required, such as milk bottles, pipes, and large containers, LDPE is used where flexibility is required, such as plastic bags and agricultural films, and LLDPE is often used in packaging films because of its good tensile and puncture resistance. Even the same HDPE is divided into injection, extrusion, and blow molding grades depending on MI (melt index)."],"sources":[{"name":"SpecialChem, comparison of PE vs PP properties","url":"https://www.specialchem.com/plastics/guide/polyethylene-versus-polypropylene"},{"name":"FDS Polymer, Polyethylene Technical Data","url":"https://fdspolimer.com/en/products/polyethylene"}]},{"id":"pp","term":"PP (Polypropylene)","ko":"polypropylene","cat":"resin","summary":"General-purpose resin with higher rigidity and heat resistance and lighter weight than PE. Changes properties to homo, random, and block copolymers.","facts":[["Density/Melting Point","0.90-0.91 g/cm³, melting point 130-171°C (depending on grade)."],["Type","Homopolymer (rigid), random copolymer (transparent/flexible), block copolymer (low-temperature impact)."],["Unit consumption","1.05 to 1.10 tons of propylene per ton of PP."]],"body":["PP is widely used in automobile interiors and exteriors, household goods, packaging, and medical devices. The crystallization rate is fast, the molding cycle is short, and the density is low, allowing the same part to be made lighter.","Instead, supplementation is needed for parts that require dimensional precision because they are vulnerable to low-temperature shock and have large mold shrinkage. Therefore, it is often used in the form of block copolymer, talc/glass fiber reinforced grade, or TPO (PP+rubber)."],"sources":[{"name":"SpecialChem, comparison of PE vs PP properties","url":"https://www.specialchem.com/plastics/guide/polyethylene-versus-polypropylene"},{"name":"Polyfluor, thermoplastic resin property table","url":"https://www.polyfluor.nl/assets/files/properties-plastics.pdf"}]},{"id":"pvc","term":"PVC (Polyvinyl Chloride)","ko":"polyvinyl chloride","cat":"resin","summary":"General-purpose resin made from chlorine and ethylene. Depending on the additive formulation, it ranges from hard pipes to soft films.","facts":[["path","Chlorine + ethylene → EDC → VCM → polymerization (suspension/emulsification) → PVC."],["Unit consumption","1.01 to 1.04 tons of VCM per ton of PVC, 1.65 tons of EDC per ton of VCM."],["Formulation","Hundreds of additives, including stabilizers, plasticizers, and fillers, are mixed to determine the intended use."]],"body":["PVC has high chlorine content, good flame retardancy, and low price, making it widely used in building materials (pipes, windows, flooring) and wire coverings. The difference in properties between rigid and flexible comes from the plasticizer formulation.","In China, the coal-based acetylene → VCM route accounts for a large portion, so crude oil and ethylene prices and Chinese PVC prices sometimes move separately. In Korea and Europe, the ethylene-based EDC route is mainstream."],"sources":[{"name":"ECVM, How is PVC Produced","url":"https://pvc.org/about-pvc/pvc-production/"},{"name":"INEOS Polymers, PVC","url":"https://www.ineos.com/industry/products/polymers/pvc/"},{"name":"S&P Global, PVC Resins CEH(2025)","url":"https://www.spglobal.com/content/dam/spglobal/ci/en/documents/products/pdf/SP_Global_CEH_Polyvinyl_Chloride_Resins_abstract_and_TOC_December_2024.pdf"}]},{"id":"ps","term":"PS / HIPS / EPS","ko":"Polystyrene series","cat":"resin","summary":"With one SM, we make transparent GPPS, HIPS mixed with rubber, and EPS mixed with gas. The price follows SM.","facts":[["GPPS","SM homopolymerization. Transparent, strong, low cost. Density 1.04~1.06 g/cm³, glass transition temperature about 100℃."],["HIPS","Improved impact resistance by grafting about 7% polybutadiene rubber onto SM (based on past data)."],["EPS","Beads containing a foaming agent such as pentane in the SM polymerization step. It is molded and foamed and used as insulation and cushioning material."],["Unit consumption","1 ton of PS and 0.93 (GP/HI) to 1.05 (EPS) tons of SM."]],"body":["The price of the PS series is relatively easy to predict because the raw material is simple and SM only. When the SM value rises, GPPS, HIPS, and EPS also rise.","GPPS is used in transparent containers, packaging, and internal parts of home appliances, HIPS is used in places subject to impact such as home appliance housings and toys, and EPS is used in building insulation and packaging cushioning materials. HIPS loses transparency as rubber is added, and its rigidity and softening point become slightly lower.","EPS is distributed in the form of beads, and foam companies inflate it with steam and mold it. Therefore, the EPS value is affected not only by the resin price but also by the operating rate and transportation costs of the foaming and molding stages."],"sources":[{"name":"Planet News, Glossary of Plastic Terms — Polystyrene","url":"http://www.plastics.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=196"},{"name":"PlasWiki, Polystyrene (PS)","url":"https://plaswiki.com/category/article/314/KO"},{"name":"OpenLearn, copolymer (SAN·HIPS·ABS)","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/science-maths-technology/chemistry/introduction-polymers/content-section-2.3.6"}]},{"id":"abs","term":"ABS","ko":"ABS resin","cat":"resin","summary":"Resin that combines the strengths of three raw materials: AN, BD, and SM. It is a representative material for home appliance housings and automobile interiors.","facts":[["Configuration","Two-phase structure in which polybutadiene rubber particles are dispersed in a SAN (styrene-acrylonitrile) matrix. More than 50% styrene."],["Division of roles","AN=heat resistance/chemical resistance, BD=impact resistance, SM=gloss/processability."],["Unit consumption","For 1 ton of ABS, SAN 0.81 + BD 0.19 (or BR 0.19), AN 0.27, SM 0.54."]],"body":["ABS is not a simple mixture of three components, but a structure in which styrene and acrylonitrile are grafted onto rubber particles. Rubber absorbs shock and the SAN matrix is ​​responsible for rigidity and surface gloss, creating properties intermediate between hard plastic and rubber.","Because of its good surface quality and coating and plating properties, it is widely used in home appliance cases, automobile interiors, toys, and office equipment. Because it has good compatibility with other resins, it is often used as a base for compounds such as PC/ABS and ABS/PBT.","The price is mainly linked to SM, which accounts for the largest proportion of the mixing ratio. However, if there is a supply disruption due to the small number of AN producers, the cost of ABS may temporarily surge and fluctuate."],"caution":"The mixing ratio (AN 23%, BD 26%, SM 55%) listed in past data was not quoted as the total was expressed as 104%. The actual mixing ratio varies depending on the grade (impact resistance, heat resistance, plating).","sources":[{"name":"INEOS Polymers, ABS","url":"https://www.ineos.com/industry/products/polymers/abs/"},{"name":"BPF, ABS and Other Specialist Styrenics","url":"https://www.bpf.co.uk/plastipedia/polymers/ABS_and_Other_Specialist_Styrenics.aspx"},{"name":"Unit table on this page — ABS","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"}]},{"id":"san","term":"SAN","ko":"Styrene-acrylonitrile copolymer","cat":"resin","summary":"Copolymer of SM and AN. It has better heat and chemical resistance than PS and maintains transparency, making it a matrix for ABS.","facts":[["Composition","AN 20-30% + SM 70-80% level (depending on grade)."],["Features","It has higher heat and chemical resistance than GPPS and is transparent. Typical uses include cosmetic containers, water purifier housing, and electronic components."],["Unit consumption","SM 0.70 + AN 0.30 tons for 1 ton of SAN, 0.81 tons of SAN for 1 ton of ABS."]],"body":["When acrylonitrile is added to polystyrene, the chains are pulled together, increasing the glass transition temperature and improving chemical resistance and surface hardness. Instead, as the proportion of AN increases, the yellowness increases, making mixing ratio management important in transparent grades.","SAN itself is used in cosmetic containers, home appliance transparent windows, and water purifier parts, and in ABS, it forms a continuous phase (matrix) and is responsible for rigidity and heat resistance."],"sources":[{"name":"OpenLearn, SAN glass transition temperature and uses","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/science-maths-technology/chemistry/introduction-polymers/content-section-2.3.6"},{"name":"BPF, ABS and Other Specialist Styrenics","url":"https://www.bpf.co.uk/plastipedia/polymers/ABS_and_Other_Specialist_Styrenics.aspx"}]},{"id":"pc","term":"PC (Polycarbonate)","ko":"Polycarbonate\nItems marked with","cat":"resin","summary":"Transparent engineering plastic made from BPA. It is used as a substitute for glass in transparent windows, electrical and electronic components, and helmet shells.","facts":[["synthesis","BPA + phosgene (interfacial method) or BPA + diphenylcarbonate (melt transesterification method)."],["Features","It is transparent, has very high impact resistance, and has a wide operating temperature range. Instead, it has weak chemical and scratch resistance."],["Unit consumption","PC is made from BPA as its main raw material, and the intensity table on this page is expressed in terms of BPA."]],"body":["Thanks to the strong chain created by the two hydroxyl groups of BPA and the carbonate bond, PC stretches and absorbs energy when impacted. Therefore, it is used where transparent and unbreakable materials are needed (bulletproof windows, helmet visors, power tool housings).","There are two commercial processes. The interfacial method is a traditional method that dissolves BPA in an organic solvent, reacts it with phosgene, and then washes and precipitates it, while the melt method removes phenol by reacting it with diphenyl carbonate without phosgene. Recently, new facilities have a large proportion of melt processes.","PC has weak chemical resistance, so crazing (microcracks) may occur when it comes in contact with certain solvents or oils. Therefore, you must first check the solvent used in the painting, adhesion, and cleaning processes."],"sources":[{"name":"Handbook of Polycarbonate Science and Technology (Process Comparison)","url":"https://api.pageplace.de/preview/DT0400.9781482273694_A38306298/preview-9781482273694_A38306298.pdf"},{"name":"Wikipedia, Polycarbonate","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polycarbonate"}]},{"id":"pbt","term":"PBT (Polybutylene Terephthalate)","ko":"PBT resin","cat":"resin","summary":"Crystalline polyester made from BDO and TPA/DMT. It is a representative engineering resin for electrical and electronic connectors and automobile parts.","facts":[["Resin","1,4-BDO + TPA (continuous method) or DMT (batch method)."],["Features","It crystallizes quickly, has a short molding cycle, and has good dimensional stability, chemical resistance, and electrical insulation. The main product is glass fiber reinforcement (GF 20-30%)."],["Unit consumption","1 ton of PBT is BDO 0.46 + TPA 0.74 (past data), the table on this page is 1,4-butadiene 0.44 + DMT 0.89."]],"body":["Among the polyester series, PBT has a fast crystallization rate, making it advantageous for injection molding. It has a low moisture absorption rate, stable dimensions, and good electrical insulation and chemical resistance, so it is often used in connectors, switches, sensor housings, and automotive electronic parts.","The process was two-pronged. There are a batch type that uses DMT and a continuous type that uses TPA. As the supply of DMT decreases, most new facilities are built using the TPA continuous method. In Korea, past batch-type facilities have been converted to other products, and the structure of importing and compounding PBT resin from Taiwan and China has grown.","The PBT value is determined between BDO and TPA. TPA has a large amount of raw materials, but BDO, which has a long process and is energy-intensive, affects the cost more."],"caution":"In the 2021-04-08 data, ‘DMT batch method → ​​TPA continuous method conversion’ and ‘domestic TPA oversupply’ are the situation at the time of writing. The PBT price (1,200 → 4,300 → $2,800/ton) in the 2021-05-17 data is also the value for the first half of that year, so do not use it as the current price.","sources":[{"name":"S&P Global, Polybutylene Terephthalate PEP Review(2022-13)","url":"https://www.spglobal.com/content/dam/spglobal/ci/en/documents/products/1025/RW2022-13_TOC.pdf"},{"name":"European Polymer Journal, PBT synthesis review (2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eurpolymj.2021.110840"}]},{"id":"pa","term":"PA6 vs PA66","ko":"Nylon 6 and Nylon 66","cat":"resin","summary":"Same nylon, but different monomers. PA66 is hotter and stronger, but has higher moisture absorption and processing difficulties.","facts":[["Monomer","PA6=1 type of caprolactam, PA66=2 types of HMDA + adipic acid."],["Melting point","PA6 approximately 215~220℃, PA66 approximately 258~260℃."],["Tensile strength","Approximately 80 to 85 MPa for PA6 and approximately 85 to 90 MPa for PA66 in dry condition (ISO 527, manufacturer data)."],["moisture absorption","PA6 absorbs more moisture at room temperature. When moisture is absorbed, dimensions increase and toughness increases, but rigidity decreases."]],"body":["Both materials have good chemical and electrical properties and are easy to process through injection and extrusion. The difference comes from the regularity of the molecular chains. PA66 has tight hydrogen bonds between amide groups, so its crystallinity and melting point are high, and its strength and heat resistance are good.","PA6 has a low melting point, a wide processing window, good surface appearance, and high toughness. However, due to the high moisture absorption rate, dimensional changes and deterioration of physical properties must be taken into account in precision parts.","The selection criteria are simple. If high temperature and high rigidity are required, use PA66 (and GF reinforcement), and if appearance, toughness, and price are important, use PA6. PA66 GF30 is common in places where heat is applied, such as under the hood of a car, and PA6 is common in household goods and textiles."],"caution":"The tensile strength in the historical data (55 MPa for PA6 and 75 MPa for PA66) is quoted from an older data and is lower than the dry value (80 to 90 MPa) in the latest manufacturer's data sheet. It varies depending on the grade and test standard, so check with TDS.","sources":[{"name":"ALBIS, PA6 vs PA66 property comparison table","url":"https://www.albis.com/dam/jcr:8d76ea1b-fad7-4dc0-91ec-79c9b4223062/PA6%20vs%20PA66_Chart_ALBIS%20PLASTIC%20GmbH.pdf"},{"name":"Mitsubishi Chemical, Nylons as Engineering Plastics","url":"https://www.mcam.com/en/products/nylons"}]},{"id":"pet","term":"PET","ko":"polyethylene terephthalate","cat":"resin","summary":"Condensation polymer of TPA and EG. Polyester is most commonly used in bottles, films, and fibers.","facts":[["Resin","TPA (or DMT) + EG. For 1 ton of PET, TPA 0.868~0.88 + EG 0.327~0.339 ton."],["Process","Esterification (or transesterification) → Condensation polymerization → Chip or direct spinning."],["Purpose","Beverage bottles, packaging films, polyester fibers, clothing and industrial yarns."]],"body":["PET is a linear polyester made by reacting TPA and EG. In order to achieve both crystallinity and transparency, products for bottles and films are rapidly cooled to an amorphous state, and crystallization for fibers is increased through stretching and heat treatment.","It is also the most established resin for recycling (PET bottle → rPET). Along with the prices of raw materials TPA and EG, supply and demand of recycled raw materials (rPET) form one axis of PET price."],"sources":[{"name":"Unit table on this page — PET","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"},{"name":"European Polymer Journal, Polyester Synthesis Review (2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eurpolymj.2021.110840"}]},{"id":"pmma","term":"PMMA","ko":"Polymethyl methacrylate (acrylic)","cat":"resin","summary":"Plastic with the highest transparency. It is used as a replacement for glass in signage, lighting covers, and automobile lamps.","facts":[["Resin","MMA (methyl methacrylate). MMA is made through several methods, including acetone, isobutylene, and ethylene."],["Features","It has a visible light transmittance comparable to that of glass and has good weather resistance. Instead, it is weak to shock and easily breaks."],["Complementary","MBS (MMA-butadiene-styrene) modifier that improves impact properties is also used."]],"body":["PMMA is called acrylic resin and has excellent transparency, surface gloss, and weather resistance, making it suitable for outdoor signs, lighting covers, and display windows. The advantage is that there is less yellowing and discoloration even when exposed to ultraviolet rays for a long period of time.","The disadvantage is brittleness. In places where impact is expected, PC can be replaced, or an impact-resistant grade that incorporates rubber components into PMMA is used.\nPlease sign using the"],"sources":[{"name":"This page petrochemical schematic — MMA·PMMA","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#petchem"},{"name":"Intensity unit table on this page — MMA (acrylic raw material)","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"}]},{"id":"pom","term":"POM (Polyacetal)","ko":"Polyacetal","cat":"resin","summary":"Crystalline resin with low friction coefficient and high rigidity. It is used in gear and bearing parts that replace metal.","facts":[["synthesis","Formaldehyde → Trioxane → Ring-opening polymerization (homopolymer) or copolymerization."],["Features","It has good dimensional stability, fatigue resistance, and chemical resistance, and has self-lubrication, making it suitable for gear and slide parts."],["Unit consumption","3 tons of formaldehyde per 1 ton of POM (unit table on this page)."]],"body":["POM has a high degree of crystallinity, making it hard and elastic, and has low friction, so it replaces metal gears, bearings, and connectors. Typical uses include automobile fuel gauges and door locks, household appliance hinges, and precision instrument parts.","It is weak to acids and gas may be generated during molding, so molding conditions and ventilation management appropriate to the grade are required."],"sources":[{"name":"Polyfluor, thermoplastic resin physical property table (POM·PET·PC)","url":"https://www.polyfluor.nl/assets/files/properties-plastics.pdf"},{"name":"Unit table on this page — Polyacetal (POM)","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"}]},{"id":"gf","term":"Glass Fiber (GF)","ko":"Glass fiber","cat":"comp","summary":"A representative reinforcing material added to plastic to increase rigidity, heat resistance, and dimensional stability. Insert into the compound in the form of chopped strands.","facts":[["form","Chopped strand (CS), which is made by bundling thousands of E-glass strands and cutting them into 3·6·12 mm, etc., is used for injection/extrusion compounds."],["Sizing","The surface of the fiber is coated with silane, etc. to achieve adhesion to the resin. Different sizing is used for each type of resin (PA, PBT, PP)."],["Reinforcement effect","When 20 to 30% of GF is added, the rigidity and heat distortion temperature increase significantly and molding shrinkage decreases."]],"body":["Glass fiber has a great reinforcing effect compared to its price, so it is included in almost all thermoplastic resin compounds such as PA, PBT, PP, and PC. The fiber length, content, and dispersion state determine the final physical properties, and the shrinkage rate in the direction perpendicular to the flow direction varies due to the fiber orientation during injection.","Data as of 2021 states that domestic production is supplied by two companies, OWENS CORNING and KCC, NEG of Japan, JUSHI·TAISAN·CPIC of China, and Taiwan Glass of Taiwan. In 2021, prices soared due to a surge in demand for wind blades and disruption in NEG sizing supply due to the Texas cold wave."],"caution":"‘Increase of more than 50% compared to the previous year’ (2021-04) and ‘Increase of 100 to 200 won/kg per month’ are the values as of 2021. You must check the current GF price and supplier structure separately.","sources":[{"name":"NEG, E-Glass Chopped Strands","url":"https://www.neg.co.jp/en/product/fiber/e-chopped_strand"},{"name":"Stariz, Chopped Strand specifications (E-glass, sizing, LOI)","url":"http://www.stariz.co.kr/cs_k.htm"},{"name":"Composites Part A, Glass fiber sizing review (2019)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compositesa.2019.105619"}]},{"id":"carbonblack","term":"Carbon Black","ko":"Carbon Black","cat":"comp","summary":"Fine carbon particles used for rubber reinforcement and black coloring. It is a key raw material for tires and plastic pigments.","facts":[["Role","Reinforcement and wear resistance in rubber, coloring, UV protection and conductivity in plastic."],["Manufacturing","The main furnace method is using incomplete combustion and pyrolysis. The raw materials are oil and natural gas."],["Domestic family tree","Domestic facility capacity is expressed as 749,000 tons/year (June 2025)."]],"body":["Carbon black has different reinforcing effects and colors depending on its particle size and structure (aggregate). For tire treads, a grade with small particles and a developed structure is used, and for plastic coloring, a grade where dispersion and color are important is used.","In plastics, it is used as a pigment that produces a deep black color, but it is also used as a functional additive to increase the weather resistance of outdoor products by absorbing ultraviolet rays."],"sources":[{"name":"This page petrochemical schematic — Carbon Black (2025.6)","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#petchem"}]},{"id":"incoterms","term":"FOB / CFR / CIF","ko":"Incoterms main conditions","cat":"trade","summary":"International trade rules that determine how much value is included. Even the same item has different FOB and CIF values.","facts":[["FOB","Seller is responsible until loading on the ship at the designated shipping port. The risk passes to the buyer upon loading on board the ship."],["CFR","The seller bears the freight from FOB to the port of destination. The point of risk transfer is FOB."],["CIF","CFR plus insurance premium. Insurance is based on minimum collateral (Institute Cargo Clauses C)."]],"body":["When comparing 'FOB China' and 'CIF Busan' in raw material estimates, you must look not only at freight and insurance costs, but also where the risk is transferred. For both CFR and CIF, the risk is transferred at the port of shipment, so if there is a problem when you arrive at the port of destination, you will argue with the insurance company and carrier, not the seller.","Many point out that FCA more realistically reflects the timing of risk transfer for container cargo than FOB. Payment terms (L/C, T/T) and inspection conditions are not determined by Incoterms and must be separately written in the contract."],"sources":[{"name":"ICC, Incoterms 2020","url":"https://iccwbo.org/business-solutions/incoterms-rules/incoterms-2020/"},{"name":"GOV.UK, Customs valuation — Incoterms","url":"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/customs-valuation/incoterms"}]},{"id":"mi","term":"MI / MFR","ko":"Melt Index (Melt Index)","cat":"trade","summary":"A measure of how well molten resin flows under standard conditions. Even the same resin is graded by MI.","facts":[["Unit","g/10min. Amount extruded at a certain temperature and load using ASTM D1238 (ISO 1133) standard orifice."],["Meaning","If the MI is high, the flow is good and the molecular weight is low. If the MI is high, the strength and impact resistance are advantageous due to the high molecular weight."],["Condition notation","Conditions for each resin are different, such as PE 190℃/2.16kg, PP 230℃/2.16kg, and PS 200℃/5kg."]],"body":["MI is not a direct value of molecular weight, but rather an empirical indicator measured under specific conditions. Therefore, MI measured at different temperatures and loads should not be compared directly, but values ​​under the same conditions should be compared.","In the field, injection, extrusion, and blow molding grades are classified by MI. For example, for injection, use high MI for good flow, and for extrusion film, use low MI that requires melt tension. Notations such as 'PC MI10' also refer to this value."],"sources":[{"name":"ASTM D1238, Melt Flow Rates standard","url":"https://www.astm.org/d1238-10.html"},{"name":"Instron, ASTM D1238 Commentary","url":"https://www.instron.com/ko/testing-solutions/astm-standards/astm-d1238/"}]},{"id":"grades","term":"Prime / Near Prime / Off Grade","ko":"Shinjae, Near Prime, Off Grade","cat":"trade","summary":"Even the same resin has different values ​​depending on the quality grade. It serves as a benchmark when looking at price competition with renewable raw materials.","facts":[["Prime(Shinjae)","A standard product from a regular process. The material property and color deviation are the smallest."],["Near Prime","A grade that is close to the standard but is traded at a lower price than the normal price due to differences in color and physical properties."],["Off Grade","Product that does not meet specifications. It has large usage limitations and has the lowest value."]],"body":["As of August 2024, the distribution price of domestic new PC materials was 2,500 to 2,600 won/kg, Chinese new materials were 100 to 200 won lower, and Chinese Off/Near Prime (MI10) offers were 1,550 to 1,600 dollars/ton (converted to 2,100 to 2,200 won/kg). There was a diagnosis that the recycled raw material business was difficult because the price difference from recycled raw materials was not large.","The grade name is not absolute as each company has different standards. Even if it is the same 'Near Prime', the color (L value), MI, and impurity content are different, so you must check the sample properties and TDS when purchasing."],"caution":"The above prices are current estimates at the time of writing on 2024-08-30. Please check the current prices of PC and recycled raw materials using the market situation table above (PC items) and supplier estimates.","sources":[{"name":"Market status table on this page — PC (polycarbonate)","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#market-quotes"}]},{"id":"unitcost","term":"Unit Consumption","ko":"Unit and cost calculation","cat":"trade","summary":"Amount of raw materials required to make 1 ton of product. Multiply by the raw material price to get the theoretical raw material cost.","facts":[["Definition","Tons of input raw materials per ton of product. The reasons for greater than 1 are yield loss, by-products, and differences in facility efficiency."],["Calculate","Raw material price (per ton) × basic unit = theoretical raw material cost per ton. Utilities, labor costs, depreciation, and margin are added to this."],["Caution","Alternative routes (BD direct / via BR) and intermediates (SAN) are listed together, so adding them as is is double counting."]],"body":["The basic unit is expressed as a range depending on the process equipment and catalyst generation. For example, 1 ton of PP contains 1.05 to 1.10 tons of propylene, and 1 ton of HDPE contains 1.02 to 1.04 tons of ethylene.","When looking at cost, raw material cost alone is not enough. By-product sales revenue (e.g. acetone from cumene-processed phenol), utility unit (steam/electricity), packaging/transportation costs, exchange rate/freight must be added together to get closer to the actual landing cost.","In the case of PBT, TPA has a large amount of raw materials, but BDO, which has a long process, has a greater cost contribution. This is why you need to look at the unit price table and raw material prices together."],"sources":[{"name":"Unit Consumption Table on this page: 90 items","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"}]},{"id":"helmet","term":"Helmet Materials","ko":"Raw materials for motorcycle helmets","cat":"app","summary":"The helmet has a dual structure of outer shell (shock dissipation) and inner foam (shock absorption). The combination of materials determines performance and price.","facts":[["Envelope","PC, ABS, FRP (fiber reinforced plastic). Selected for the balance of impact resistance, light weight, and appearance."],["Shock absorbing layer","EPS (expanded polystyrene). Crushes with one impact and absorbs energy."],["Lining/Strap","Moisture-absorbing and breathable materials such as polyester and Coolmax, and nylon straps and buckles."]],"body":["A helmet's performance comes from its structure rather than the material itself. The hard shell disperses the impact widely, and the EPS underneath collapses, reducing the acceleration transmitted to the head. Therefore, once a helmet has been hit hard, the EPS has already been crushed and must be replaced.","PC is advantageous for transparency and high impact, ABS is advantageous for processability and price, and FRP is advantageous for high rigidity and light weight. Recently, PC/ABS blends and carbon/glass fiber composites are also used."],"sources":[{"name":"Unit table on this page — PS (EPS), ABS, PC","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#unit-consumption"}]},{"id":"applications","term":"Applications","ko":"Home appliance, automobile, and packaging application map","cat":"app","summary":"Application map to see at a glance which resin goes where. The material of the same part changes depending on the required performance.","facts":[["Home appliances","ABS·HIPS housing, PC transparent window, PP internal parts, PS packaging."],["Car","PP bumper/interior, PA66 GF underhood, PBT connector, PC lamp cover."],["Packaging","PET bottle, PE film, EPS cushioning, PP container."],["Architecture","PVC pipes/windows, EPS/XPS insulation, PC sheets."]],"body":["Material selection is a triangle of performance, price, and processability. For example, for home appliance housings, ABS is chosen because its appearance and paintability are important; for transparent windows, PC or PMMA is chosen; and for internal structures, low-cost PP is chosen.","If there are requirements such as flame retardancy, heat resistance, and weather resistance, the grade of the same resin will change and the cost will increase. It is safe to first check the requirements of the component specifications and then verify them with the TDS of the appropriate grade."],"sources":[{"name":"This page petrochemical schematic (product flow)","url":"https://insightbriefnews.com/market.html#petchem"}]},{"id":"iron-ore","term":"Iron Ore","ko":"Iron ore and Fe 62%","cat":"steel","summary":"This is the starting point of steel. Pig iron is made by reducing iron ore to coke, and 98% of mined iron ore is used as a raw material for steel.","facts":[["International standard product","Iron ore prices are quoted based on 62% iron content as a benchmark. If the quality is low, the price per ton is discounted, and if there are a lot of impurities such as moisture, alumina, and phosphorus, the steelmaking intensity increases."],["Input per ton of crude steel","The blast furnace/converter route costs 1,370kg of iron ore, 780kg of coking coal, 270kg of limestone, and 125kg of iron scrap (World Steel Association average)."],["1 ton of pig iron","It costs 1.6 tons of iron ore and about 450 kg of coke. Some of the coke can be replaced by pulverized coal injection (PCI)."]],"body":["Iron ore is not put into the blast furnace as is. The powder is mixed with sintered ore or pellets to ensure breathability, then mixed with coke and limestone and charged into the blast furnace. Inside the blast furnace, molten iron (pig iron) flows downward as the carbon in the coke removes the oxygen from the iron oxide.","The iron ore price seen by steel companies is based on the CFR Chinese quote price for Fe 62% standard product. Actual procurement involves price adjustments depending on quality, moisture, and impurities, and involves a high proportion of long-term contracts with mines and traders.","When the price of iron ore rises, the cost of blast furnaces reacts first, and for electric furnaces, we look at the price of iron scrap. The price difference between the two raw materials determines the cost competitiveness of each steelmaker."],"caution":"Fe 62% is based on the market quote and not the contract value. You must check the Fe standard, moisture correction, and impurity upper limit in the contract to calculate the actual unit.","sources":[{"name":"World Steel, Raw materials","url":"https://worldsteel.org/about-steel/raw-materials/"},{"name":"World Steel Association, Steel and raw materials fact sheet (2023)","url":"https://worldsteel.org/wp-content/uploads/Fact-sheet-raw-materials-2023-1.pdf"}]},{"id":"bf-bof","term":"Blast Furnace · BOF","ko":"Blast furnace/converter integrated steel production","cat":"steel","summary":"This is the representative route to make steel by refining pig iron, which is iron ore reduced to coke, with oxygen in a converter. Approximately 70% of the world's crude steel comes from this route.","facts":[["Input 1,000kg of crude steel","1,370 kg of iron ore, 780 kg of metallurgical coal, 270 kg of limestone, 125 kg of iron scrap (World Steel Association)."],["World share","The blast furnace/converter (BF/BOF) route accounts for approximately 70% of global crude steel production, and the electric furnace accounts for approximately 30%."],["The role of the converter","Oxygen is blown into the pig iron to burn carbon, and scrap is charged together up to around 30% to adjust the temperature and composition."]],"body":["A blast furnace is a facility that does not stop working 24 hours a day. Once operation begins, raw materials are continuously added and pig iron is extracted throughout the life of the furnace (usually 15 to 20 years). Therefore, even if the demand for crude steel decreases, blast furnaces cannot be easily built.","In the converter, the carbon in pig iron is burned with oxygen to reduce it to around 0.1%, and alloy elements are added to adjust the steel grade. Afterwards, slabs, billets, and blooms are created through continuous casting.","This route is advantageous for mass production, but the cost greatly depends on the price of coking coal and iron ore, and the cost of carbon emissions. In Korea, POSCO and Hyundai Steel integrated steel mills use this route."],"caution":"The blast furnace/converter input amount is the average of the World Steel Association. In actual steel mills, the unit price varies depending on the quality of raw materials, scrap input rate, and operating conditions.","sources":[{"name":"World Steel, Raw materials","url":"https://worldsteel.org/about-steel/raw-materials/"},{"name":"World Steel Association, Steel and raw materials fact sheet (2023)","url":"https://worldsteel.org/wp-content/uploads/Fact-sheet-raw-materials-2023-1.pdf"}]},{"id":"eaf","term":"Electric Arc Furnace","ko":"Electric Furnace (EAF)","cat":"steel","summary":"This is the route to make steel by melting iron scrap with electrodes. It is the center of long section steel production for construction, and has lower carbon emissions than a blast furnace.","facts":[["Input 1,000kg of crude steel","710 kg of iron scrap, 586 kg of iron ore, 150 kg of coal, 88 kg of limestone, 2.3 GJ of electricity (World Steel Association)."],["Global/domestic proportion","Approximately 30% of the world's crude steel comes from electric arc furnaces. The proportion of electric arc furnace steel in domestic crude steel was 28.5% in May 2026 (Korea Steel Association)."],["Main products","The proportion of long products used in construction, such as rebar, section steel, and wire rod, is high, making it sensitive to the construction market."]],"body":["Electric furnaces melt scrap by passing a large electric current through graphite electrodes. Since the raw materials are scrap, management of impurities such as copper and tin determines quality. It is difficult to make high-quality steel if you use a lot of lightweight scrap with a lot of impurities.","Recently, the use of direct reduction iron (DRI) or molten iron in electric furnaces to improve quality is increasing. The policy to increase the proportion of electricity as one of the pillars of steel decarbonization also targets this path.","The cost is determined by the price of steel scrap and electricity charges. This is why we avoid fishing during times of high power usage."],"caution":"The proportion of electric furnaces varies quarterly depending on the construction market and electricity prices. The above 28.5% is based on crude steel production as of May 2026.","sources":[{"name":"World Steel, Raw materials","url":"https://worldsteel.org/about-steel/raw-materials/"},{"name":"Korea Steel Association, Current Status of Steel Industry","url":"https://www.kosa.or.kr/sub/steel_info/sub02_3.jsp"}]},{"id":"steel-scrap","term":"Steel Scrap","ko":"Iron Scrap","cat":"steel","summary":"It is the main raw material for electric furnaces and a renewable iron source that is also used as an auxiliary input in blast furnaces and converters. Grade and impurities determine price.","facts":[["World Usage","In 2021, the global steel industry used approximately 680 million tons of recycled steel as raw material (World Steel Association)."],["Rating","In domestic distribution, it is divided into heavy weight (thick plate), new material (generated at the factory), and light weight (household scrap). The thicker the material, the higher the melting yield and the higher the value."],["Quality variables","If there is a lot of non-ferrous metals such as copper, tin, and zinc, the impurities in the electric furnace steel rise, making it difficult to produce high-quality steel."]],"body":["Steel scrap is divided into scrap iron (old iron) produced at the end of the life of steel products and factory scrap produced directly from the steelmaking and rolling process. Factory scrap has a high value because its composition is known, and household scrap metal incurs a sorting fee.","Electric furnace steel mills charge mixed scrap grades. Using a lot of cheap scrap lowers the cost, but the product grade may have to be lowered due to impurities.","There is high domestic demand for steel scrap, so the proportion of imports is high, and Japanese and US scrap prices and exchange rates affect domestic bid prices."],"sources":[{"name":"World Steel Association, Steel and raw materials fact sheet (2023)","url":"https://worldsteel.org/wp-content/uploads/Fact-sheet-raw-materials-2023-1.pdf"},{"name":"World Steel, Raw materials","url":"https://worldsteel.org/about-steel/raw-materials/"}]},{"id":"flat-steel","term":"HR · CR","ko":"Hot-rolled and cold-rolled steel sheets","cat":"steel","summary":"Hot rolling is made by rolling a slab at high temperature, and cold rolling is rolling it again at room temperature. It is a basic material for automobiles, home appliances, and architectural thin plates.","facts":[["Specifications","Hot rolled mild steel sheets and strips are regulated by KS D 3501, and cold rolled steel sheets and strips are regulated by KS D 3512."],["Process differences","Hot rolling involves reheating slabs, rolling them at high temperatures, and wrapping them into coils. Cold rolling involves pickling hot rolled coils to remove scale and then rolling them again at room temperature."],["Surface/Precision","Cold rolled steel has small thickness variation and surface roughness, making it suitable as a painting and plating material, while hot rolled steel is widely used as structural material, pipe material, and pickling material."]],"body":["Hot rolled (HR) is thick and leaves mill scale on the surface. In some cases, it is used as is, but in most cases, the scale is removed through pickling and sent to cold rolled or plated materials.","Cold rolling (CR) goes through annealing and temper rolling after rolling to adjust the processability and surface. It is used in areas where surface quality is important, such as car exteriors, home appliance sheet metal, furniture, and electronic parts.","Even if the thickness is the same, hot-rolled, cold-rolled, and plated materials have different dimensional tolerances and surface grades, so steel grade and surface treatment must be specified in the order to prevent other materials from being sent."],"sources":[{"name":"Korean Standards Association, KS D 3501 Hot rolled mild steel sheets and strips","url":"https://www.standard.go.kr/KSCI/standardIntro/getStandardSearchView.do?menuId=919&topMenuId=137&upperMenuId=504&ksNo=KSD3501"},{"name":"Korean Standards Association, KS D 3512 Cold rolled steel sheets and strips","url":"https://www.standard.go.kr/KSCI/standardIntro/getStandardSearchView.do?menuId=919&topMenuId=137&upperMenuId=504&ksNo=KSD3512"}]},{"id":"galvanized","term":"GI · GA","ko":"Hot dip galvanized steel sheet","cat":"steel","summary":"This is a steel plate that is protected from corrosion by coating the steel surface with zinc. The iron does not rust even if scratched due to the sacrificial anode action where the zinc corrodes first.","facts":[["Specifications","Hot-dip galvanized steel sheets and strips are specified in KS D 3506."],["GI and GA","GI is a plate dipped in a zinc bath and immediately cooled, while GA is a plate made by plating and heat treatment to create a zinc-iron alloy layer. GA is widely used in automobiles because of its good paint adhesion and weldability."],["Plating amount notation","It is expressed as the amount of zinc adhesion on both sides, such as Z08, Z12, Z18, and Z27. The larger the number, the thicker and longer the corrosion resistance."]],"body":["Zinc has a greater tendency to ionize than iron, so even if the plating layer is scratched, zinc melts first and protects the iron. This sacrificial anode action is the key to the corrosion resistance of plated steel sheets.","GI is used for building exteriors, roofs, and ducts, and GA or electrogalvanizing (EGI) is used for automobile bodies. EGI has a small amount of plating adhesion, but the surface is flat and the painting quality is good.","If the plating amount and post-processing (phosphate, oil, resin) are not adjusted to the application, the plating may peel off during processing or weldability may deteriorate."],"sources":[{"name":"Korean Standards Association, KS D 3506 Hot-dip galvanized steel sheets and strips","url":"https://www.standard.go.kr/KSCI/standardIntro/getStandardSearchView.do?menuId=919&topMenuId=137&upperMenuId=504&ksNo=KSD3506"},{"name":"POSCO, electrogalvanized steel product information (PDF)","url":"https://www.posco.co.kr/homepage/docs/kor5/dn/product/info/electrogalvanizedsteel.pdf"}]},{"id":"rebar","term":"Rebar SD400","ko":"Rebar","cat":"steel","summary":"This is a deformed bar for reinforced concrete. It is a representative product of electric furnace steel manufacturers and is directly linked to domestic construction demand.","facts":[["Specifications","Steel bars for reinforced concrete are specified in KS D 3504, and SD400 has a yield strength of 400 MPa."],["notation","It is called the nominal diameter, such as D10~D57, and the number after SD refers to the design yield strength."],["Demand","It goes into the framework and foundation of construction sites, and the shipment volume moves with the construction market."]],"body":["The nodes (ribs) on the surface of the reinforcing bar serve to increase adhesion to concrete. So, instead of smooth round bars, we use deformed bars.","SD400 is most widely used in general construction and civil engineering, and SD500 and higher are used in high-rises and bridges. As the steel grade rises, it receives a greater load with the same cross section.","Domestic rebar is mainly produced by electric arc furnace steel manufacturers. The price of steel scrap, electricity costs, and construction start volume determine the price."],"sources":[{"name":"Korean Standards Association, KS D 3504 Steel bars for reinforced concrete","url":"https://www.standard.go.kr/KSCI/standardIntro/getStandardSearchView.do?menuId=919&topMenuId=137&upperMenuId=504&ksNo=KSD3504"}]},{"id":"stainless","term":"STS 304 · 316","ko":"stainless steel","cat":"steel","summary":"It is a steel with more than 10.5% of chromium added to create a self-healing film on the surface. 304 is general purpose, 316 is resistant to salt and acid due to the addition of molybdenum.","facts":[["basic composition","304 is a representative austenitic type with 18% chromium and 8% nickel. 316 adds 2-3% molybdenum to it."],["Specific gravity","Austenitic accounts for more than 65% of global stainless steel usage."],["Cost","Nickel and molybdenum prices largely determine the cost, so we look at the LME nickel price and the alloy raw material premium together."]],"body":["The key to stainless steel is the passive film created by chromium combining with oxygen. Even if the surface is scratched, the film regenerates and corrosion does not occur.","304 is widely used in cooking utensils, food equipment, building finishes, and washing machine drums, while 316 is used in areas exposed to chlorides and acids, such as marine structures, chemical facilities, and medical equipment.","The 300 series contains nickel and is non-magnetic, but the 400 series ferrite series contains only chromium without nickel, making it different in magnetism and price competitiveness. Just because a magnet sticks in the field should not be considered a defect."],"caution":"STS 304·316 is the nominal composition of the representative grade. The actual ingredient range varies depending on KS·ASTM·EN standards and steel mill product tables.","sources":[{"name":"worldstainless, Categories, grades and product forms","url":"https://worldstainless.org/about-stainless/what-are-stainless-steels/categories-grades-and-product-forms/"}]},{"id":"copper-cathode","term":"Copper Cathode","ko":"Electric building","cat":"steel","summary":"It is a pure copper plate made by smelting and electrolyzing copper ore. It is the starting raw material for wires, copper tubes, and copper foil, and is the physical standard for LME copper prices.","facts":[["LME specifications","Grade A electrolytic copper follows the Cu-CATH-1 standard, and the total impurities specified are less than 0.0065%, so the purity is expressed at around 99.99%."],["Contract Unit","LME copper futures lots are 25 tonnes and quoted in USD/tonne."],["Purpose","Demand for copper and copper alloy products in the United States is 42% from construction, 23% from electricity and electronics, and 18% from transportation (USGS, cited by the Copper Development Association)."]],"body":["Copper copper is melted in a furnace to create blister copper, and an electric current is passed between the anode and cathode in an electrolyzer to obtain a highly pure cathode plate. This plate is electric copper.","Electrical copper is cast into wire rods and pulled into wires, or processed into copper pipes, brass, and copper alloys. Recently, demand for copper foil for negative electrode current collectors in secondary batteries has increased.","The LME price is the international standard price, and the domestic Public Procurement Service release price and domestic distribution price are subject to premium, exchange rate, and value-added tax."],"caution":"LME prices are standard prices excluding tariffs, freight rates, and regional premiums. The domestic arrival cost must be calculated by adding freight, insurance, exchange rate, and tariffs.","sources":[{"name":"LME, Copper Grade A chemical composition specifications","url":"https://www.lme.com/-/media/Files/Physical-services/Brands/Chemical-composition/Chemical-composition-Copper.pdf"},{"name":"USGS, Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — Copper","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-copper.pdf"}]},{"id":"lme-base-metals","term":"LME Base Metals","ko":"LME Non-ferrous Metals Trading","cat":"steel","summary":"It is the international standard market for copper, aluminum, zinc, lead, nickel, tin, and cobalt. The price is USD/ton, and payment is based on 3-month futures.","facts":[["Lot size","25 tons of copper, aluminum, zinc, and lead, 6 tons of nickel, 5 tons of tin, and 1 ton of cobalt."],["3 month gift","The LME price is based on 3-month contract (3M), and the difference between spot and 3-month contract is called backwardation (overvaluation of spot) and contango (undervaluation of spot)."],["Inventory and premium","LME warehouse inventory and regional delivery premiums move separately, so the physical price of the same metal varies depending on the delivery region."]],"body":["The LME operates a network of warehouses that deliver physical metals, as well as an over-the-counter futures market. Refinery brands must be LME approved for warehouse delivery, and this list of approved brands becomes the quality standard for physical transactions.","In practice, a CIF quote is created by adding a premium to the LME 3-month price. Premiums can run up to hundreds of dollars depending on local availability, freight, and duty refunds.","In China, SHFE prices move separately. The difference (arbitrage) between international prices and Chinese domestic prices also creates import and export flows."],"caution":"LME prices are international standards per tonne. Premium, freight, exchange rate, tariff, and value-added tax must be added to the domestic import cost.","sources":[{"name":"LME, A Guide to the London Metal Exchange(2022)","url":"https://www.lme.com/-/media/Files/Education/Online-resources/Brochures/A-Guide-to-the-LME-2022.pdf"},{"name":"LME, Copper Grade A chemical composition specifications","url":"https://www.lme.com/-/media/Files/Physical-services/Brands/Chemical-composition/Chemical-composition-Copper.pdf"}]},{"id":"aluminium","term":"Aluminium","ko":"Aluminum","cat":"steel","summary":"It is a lightweight metal made by extracting alumina from bauxite and electrolysis. Because it requires a lot of power, electricity bills account for a large portion of the cost.","facts":[["Input of raw materials","From 4 to 6 tons of bauxite, 2 tons of alumina and 1 ton of primary aluminum are produced (International Aluminum Association)."],["Electricity intensity","The electrolysis process requires approximately 14,000 kWh of power per ton. There is also data that puts it at 14,000 to 16,000 kWh (Geoscience Australia)."],["Machining","It is divided into rolled sheets (cans, automobiles), extruded materials (windows, frames), die casting (parts), and foil (packaging, secondary battery current collector)."]],"body":["Bauxite is dissolved with caustic soda to extract alumina (Bayer process), and alumina is dissolved in cryolite and electrolyzed (Hall-Eru process) to produce primary aluminum. In this process, a large amount of electricity is used, so aluminum is sometimes called ‘solid electricity’.","Primary aluminum is cast into billets and slabs and sent to extrusion and rolling mills. Secondary aluminum is made by re-melting scrap, and as it requires much less power than primary aluminum, its importance is increasing in terms of decarbonization.","The demand is wide, ranging from lightweight automobiles, cans, building windows and doors, power cables, and secondary battery collectors, so the sensitivity to economic conditions is relatively low."],"sources":[{"name":"International Aluminium Institute, Aluminium carbon footprint FAQs","url":"https://international-aluminium.org/landing/aluminium-carbon-footprint-faqs/"},{"name":"Geoscience Australia, Aluminium","url":"https://www.ga.gov.au/education/minerals-energy/australian-mineral-facts/aluminium"}]},{"id":"zinc","term":"Zinc","ko":"Zinc","cat":"steel","summary":"It is a key metal in steel plating. Approximately 60% of global zinc consumption is used to plating steel to prevent corrosion.","facts":[["Purpose Structure","Global consumption of refined zinc is approximately 60% from plating, 15% from die casting, 9% from brass and bronze, 11% from compounds, and 4% from semi-finished products (ILZSG·IZA)."],["Transaction Unit","LME zinc futures lots are 25 tonnes and quoted at USD/tonne."],["Domestic price","Domestic zinc ingot domestic sales price and Public Procurement Service emission price are in the market situation table on this page."]],"body":["Zinc concentrate is roasted and sintered and then refined by electrolysis or ISP (vertical furnace) method to create zinc ingots. Zinc ingots are used as raw materials for plating baths, die casting alloys, and brass.","Zinc plating takes advantage of the property of zinc to corrode before iron. Even if the plating layer is scratched, the surrounding zinc melts and the sacrificial anode function protects the iron, greatly increasing the lifespan of bridges, towers, and automobile bodies.","Zinc moves along with demand for construction and automobiles, and interruptions in mine supply or smelter production cuts can greatly affect prices."],"sources":[{"name":"ILZSG, The World Zinc Factbook 2024","url":"https://www.ilzsg.org/wp-content/uploads/SitePDFs/The%20World%20Zinc%20Factbook%202024.pdf"},{"name":"LME, A Guide to the London Metal Exchange(2022)","url":"https://www.lme.com/-/media/Files/Education/Online-resources/Brochures/A-Guide-to-the-LME-2022.pdf"}]},{"id":"nickel","term":"Nickel","ko":"Nickel","cat":"steel","summary":"It is a key raw material for 300 series stainless steel and secondary battery cathode material precursor. The LME nickel price is the standard for stainless steel and battery costs.","facts":[["LME specifications","LME nickel is traded in 6-ton lots with a minimum purity of 99.80%."],["Purpose","More than 85% of U.S. nickel consumption goes to stainless steel, alloy steel, and nickel alloy (USGS 2026). The rest are electroplating, batteries, catalysts, and chemistry."],["Ore","It is divided into laterite (oxidized ore) and sulfide ore, and China processes a large portion of Indonesian and Philippine laterite into NPI (nickel pig iron)."]],"body":["Nickel is an element that stabilizes the austenite structure in stainless steel. 8-14% goes into 300 series such as 304 and 316, and when nickel prices rise, there is a movement to replace it with 200 series or 400 series.","In batteries, it is processed into nickel sulfate and added to the cathode material precursor. The higher the nickel cathode material, the greater the nickel input, creating a new demand for batteries in the nickel market.","LME nickel has become more volatile since the 2022 short squeeze, and oversupply has continued since 2022 due to increased supply from Indonesia (USGS)."],"sources":[{"name":"LME, A Guide to the London Metal Exchange(2022)","url":"https://www.lme.com/-/media/Files/Education/Online-resources/Brochures/A-Guide-to-the-LME-2022.pdf"},{"name":"USGS, Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — Nickel","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-nickel.pdf"}]},{"id":"soybean-crush","term":"Soybean Crush","ko":"Soybean Crushing","cat":"agri","summary":"This is a process that separates soybeans into soybean meal and soybean oil by pressing and solvent extracting them. The crush margin is the combined value of the two products minus the soybean price and processing costs.","facts":[["Yield per bushel","Based on USDA 2025/26, 1 bushel (60 lb) of soybeans yields 47.4 lb of soybean meal and 11.62 lb of soybean oil."],["Market Practices","Calculations of 78 to 80% for Park, 18 to 20% for Yu, and 1 to 2% for loss and blood are widely used."],["Crush Margin","It is calculated as soybean meal"]],"body":["Soybeans are a crop that extracts both protein and oil. Therefore, the price of soybeans is determined by the demand in both markets: soybean meal and soybean oil.","The pressing process breaks the soybeans into pieces, heats them, and extracts the oil with a solvent. The remaining gourds are used as feed, and the oil is refined and used as cooking oil or biodiesel raw material.","If the demand for biodiesel and HVO increases, the price of soybean oil rises, and if crushing increases, the supply of soybean meal also increases, suppressing the meal price."],"sources":[{"name":"USDA ERS, Oil Crops Outlook(2026.3)","url":"https://ers.usda.gov/media/20862/ocs-26c.pdf"},{"name":"USDA ERS, Soybeans and Oil Crops","url":"https://www.ers.usda.gov/topics/crops/soybeans-and-oil-crops/"}]},{"id":"soybean-meal","term":"Soybean Meal","ko":"Soybean meal","cat":"agri","summary":"It is a high-protein feed ingredient that remains after removing the oil from soybeans. It is used as the protein standard for livestock compound feed.","facts":[["Protein","The market standard product is a product with 44% or 48% crude protein, and the 48% product is a high-protein feed and is expensive."],["Extraction rate","USDA estimates the 2025/26 U.S. soybean meal extraction rate at 47.4 lb per bushel."],["Substitutes","The mixing ratio changes depending on DDGS, canola meal, and palm meal and price."]],"body":["Soybean meal has a good composition of essential amino acids and is used as the main protein source in pig and chicken feed. For ruminants, feed mixed with DDGS or other cucurbits.","Soybean meal prices are sensitive to soybean crushing volume, South American crop conditions, and feed demand in China. If China adjusts its feed mix, global soybean meal prices will immediately fluctuate.","When importing soybean meal for feed, the tariff and quarantine conditions differ depending on the product, so you must check the feed grade and ingredient specifications before signing a contract."],"sources":[{"name":"USDA ERS, Oil Crops Outlook(2026.3)","url":"https://ers.usda.gov/media/20862/ocs-26c.pdf"}]},{"id":"soybean-oil","term":"Soybean Oil","ko":"Soybean oil","cat":"agri","summary":"It is a vegetable oil extracted from soybeans. It is used as cooking oil, and recently, demand for biodiesel and HVO raw materials has driven up prices.","facts":[["Extraction rate","The USDA 2025/26 soybean oil extraction rate is 11.62 lb per bushel."],["Purpose","After refining, it is used in cooking oil, margarine, and processed foods, and also as a raw material for biodiesel and renewable diesel (HVO)."],["Contention","Its uses overlap with palm oil, canola oil, and sunflower oil, and the mix of raw materials changes depending on policies and crop conditions."]],"body":["Soybean oil is widely used as cooking oil due to its high linoleic acid content. During the refining process, gums (saponifiables), pigments, and odors are removed to make RBD oil.","In the United States, as demand for renewable diesel (HVO) and biodiesel raw materials grows, soybean oil is directly connected to the energy market. So crude oil prices and biofuel policy work together on soybean oil prices.","Because food and energy compete for the same raw materials, changes in biofuel mandates also affect the price of cooking oil."],"sources":[{"name":"USDA ERS, Oil Crops Outlook(2026.3)","url":"https://ers.usda.gov/media/20862/ocs-26c.pdf"}]},{"id":"corn-ethanol","term":"Corn Ethanol · DDGS","ko":"Corn Ethanol and DDGS","cat":"agri","summary":"Corn starch is fermented to make ethanol, and the remaining protein and fat are recovered as feed called DDGS.","facts":[["Yield per bushel","One bushel (56 lb) of corn yields 2.8 gallons of fuel ethanol and 17 lb of DDGS."],["Parts of use","Only starch (about 70% of the grain) is converted to ethanol, while proteins, fats, and minerals are concentrated in DDGS."],["Feed value","DDGS is a feed that replaces the corn + soybean meal mix, and the mix ratio is adjusted depending on the price."]],"body":["A dry grind plant grinds corn, ferments it with water and yeast, and distills ethanol. The remaining liquid is dried and made into DDGS.","DDGS produced when making one gallon of ethanol is supplied back to the feed market, so as ethanol production increases, feed supply also increases. This is the link between corn and soybean meal prices.","The United States created demand for corn ethanol through the Renewable Fuel Mandate (RFS), and Brazil uses sugarcane ethanol. Raw material harvests and policies determine ethanol margins."],"sources":[{"name":"Purdue Extension, How Fuel Ethanol Is Made from Corn","url":"https://www.agmrc.org/media/cms/ID328_68C00C7BFC13F.pdf"},{"name":"Extension, Corn for Biofuel Production","url":"https://farm-energy.extension.org/corn-for-biofuel-production/"}]},{"id":"wheat-flour","term":"Wheat Flour","ko":"Wheat milling and light/gravity/strong flour","cat":"agri","summary":"Wheat is milled and divided into confectionery, noodle, and bakery purposes according to its protein content. The quantity and quality of gluten determines its use.","facts":[["Protein classification","It is about 7 to 9% soft flour, 9 to 11% medium flour, and 11 to 13% strong flour. The same density varies depending on the variety and grade."],["gluten","Glutenin (elasticity) and gliadin (extensibility) combine with water to create a network, making the dough viscoelastic."],["Milling rate","The percentage of flour produced from the whole wheat ranges from 60 to 75% depending on the variety and grade."]],"body":["Milling begins with tempering, where water is added to the wheat to make it easier to separate the husk and endosperm. Afterwards, grinding, sieving, and regrinding are repeated to adjust the particle size and ash content.","Cake flour has weak gluten and is used in crispy and soft products such as cakes and cookies, all-purpose flour is used in noodles, udon, and dumpling skins, and strong flour is used in products that require elasticity and gas retention, such as bread and ramen.","For ramen, use medium-strength flour with around 12% protein, and for noodles, around 10% protein is appropriate. Even if it is the same ‘gravity flour’, the protein and ash content varies depending on the mill, so the mix must be adjusted."],"caution":"Protein classification is a representative range for commercially available flours. You must check the miller’s product list for specifications and ash content for each product.","sources":[{"name":"Journal of Korean Breeding Society, Flour protein and ash analysis (2016)","url":"https://doi.org/10.9787/kjbs.2016.48.4.442"}]},{"id":"rice-milling","term":"Rice Milling","ko":"Rice polishing","cat":"agri","summary":"The husk is removed from the rice plant to make brown rice, and the bran layer and germ are removed to make white rice. The degree of polishing determines the yield and taste of rice.","facts":[["Je Hyeon-yul","The ratio of rice to brown rice is 78-80%."],["Hyunbaek Ratio","The ratio of brown rice to white rice is 90-93%, and the theoretical whitening rate is 92% (10 minutes)."],["Final yield","70 to 75 kg of white rice is produced from 100 kg of rice."]],"body":["Polishing is carried out in the following order: Jehyun (removal of rice husks), rice polishing (removal of rice bran layer), and fine rice sorting (sorting of snail and color). In fact, rice processing plants (RPC) process rice in less than 12 minutes.","The more rice is polished, the whiter the rice and the softer the taste, but the yield decreases and the nutritional content decreases. On the other hand, if you cut it less, a layer of rice bran may remain and storage capacity may be reduced.","Rice husk, rice bran, and husk are resold as feed, compost, and biomass. Utilization of milling by-products offsets part of the cost of rice processing."],"sources":[{"name":"Post-harvest rice management and polishing by Rural Development Administration","url":"https://www.nongsaro.go.kr/portal/ps/psx/psxa/mlrdCurationDtl.mo?curationNo=65&menuId=PS03974&totalSearchYn=Y"}]},{"id":"raw-sugar","term":"Raw Sugar No.11","ko":"Raw sugar No.11","cat":"agri","summary":"International benchmark for raw sugar cane sugar. ICE No. 11 futures sets the price of raw sugar before refining, and the refinery processes it again into white sugar.","facts":[["Contract Unit","ICE Raw Sugar No. 11 is a 112,000 lb (50 long tons, approximately 50.8 tons) contract."],["Quality standards","Centrifuged raw sugar with an average pole of 96 degrees is the Indian standard, and the higher the pole, the higher the premium."],["Tablets","Raw sugar is melted, impurities are removed, and recrystallized to make white sugar, sugar cubes, and liquid sugar."]],"body":["Raw sugar is an intermediate product obtained by pressing sugar cane, extracting the juice, and concentrating and crystallizing it. Since the sugar content (pol) is around 96 degrees, it is not eaten as is, but is re-processed with white sugar at a refinery.","Molasses from the refining process is used as fermentation raw material and feed, and Brazil, which directly ferments sugarcane juice, switches between ethanol production and sugar production depending on price.","International raw sugar prices are sensitive to crop conditions, ethanol conversion rates, and export policies in Brazil, India, and Thailand."],"sources":[{"name":"ICE, Sugar No.11 Contract Specification","url":"https://www.ice.com/api/productguide/spec/23/pdf"},{"name":"ICE Futures U.S., Sugar No.11 Rules","url":"https://www.ice.com/publicdocs/rulebooks/futures_us/11_Sugar_11.pdf"}]},{"id":"coffee","term":"Arabica · Robusta","ko":"Green coffee beans","cat":"agri","summary":"Two species of coffee, Arabica and Robusta, account for most of world production. Caffeine, flavor, and growing conditions are different.","facts":[["Caffeine","Arabica green coffee beans are 0.9-1.4% and Robusta 1.7-4.0%, which is about twice that of Robusta."],["Production share","Of the 178 million bags (60 kg) of global production in 2023/24, 57.4% were Arabica and 42.6% Robusta (ICO)."],["Transaction Unit","International transactions are based on 60kg bags, and futures use ICE Arabica/Robusta contracts."]],"body":["Arabica grows at cool altitudes of 1,000 to 2,000 meters above sea level and has rich acidity and aroma. Robusta grows in lowlands from 0 to 700 m and has a strong bitter taste and body, so it is often used in instant and blends.","Green coffee beans are roasted to create their scent and color, and then go through grinding and extraction to make cafe drinks or instant coffee. The degree of roasting and extraction method can greatly change the taste of the same coffee bean.","Coffee prices are sensitive to crop conditions in Brazil and Vietnam, frost and drought, exchange rates, and freight rates. Green coffee beans are graded based on screen size and number of defective coffee beans, but the notation varies from country to country, so you need to check the contract."],"sources":[{"name":"International Coffee Organization, Coffee Report and Outlook(2023.12)","url":"https://ico.org/documents/cy2023-24/Coffee_Report_and_Outlook_December_2023_ICO.pdf"}]},{"id":"palm-oil","term":"Crude Palm Oil","ko":"Palm oil CPO·PKO","cat":"agri","summary":"It is crude oil squeezed from palm fruit. It is a common raw material for cooking oil, oleochemicals, and biodiesel, and its oil production per unit area is the highest among vegetable oils.","facts":[["Milking rate","The Malaysian palm oil extraction rate (OER) was 19.86% in 2023. About 20% of the fruit's weight is crude oil."],["Fruit yield","The palm fruit yield in the same year was 15.79 tonnes per ha (MPOB)."],["By-products","Palm kernel oil (PKO) is extracted from palm kernels, and after milking, the shoots and bark are used as fuel and compost."]],"body":["Crude oil (CPO) is produced by steaming the palm fruit, separating the flesh, and pressing it. CPO is red and contains a lot of carotene, so it is made into edible oil after refining, bleaching, and deodorizing (RBD).","CPO goes not only to cooking oil, but also to oil chemical raw materials such as fatty acids and glycerin, soap, cosmetics, and biodiesel and HVO raw materials. Because of its wide range of uses, food demand and energy demand compete for the same raw materials.","Indonesia and Malaysia lead production, and export taxes, export quotas, and sustainability certification (EU regulations) affect price and volume."],"sources":[{"name":"MPOB, Overview of the Malaysian Oil Palm Industry 2023","url":"https://palmoilis.mpob.gov.my/files/2024/10/Overview2023.pdf"}]},{"id":"natural-rubber","term":"TSR20 · RSS3","ko":"Natural rubber grade","cat":"agri","summary":"Natural rubber is traded in smoked sheets (RSS) and blocks (TSR). Most tires are made of raw materials, and the degree of contamination and viscosity varies depending on the grade.","facts":[["TSR20 specification","Thailand STR20 standards include pollution level of 0.16% or less, ash content of 0.8% or less, nitrogen content of 0.6% or less, volatile content of 0.8% or less, initial firing rate of 30 or more, and firing maintenance index of 40 or more."],["RSS3","This is a visual grade that determines the smoke sheet by eye, and is used for tires, tubes, and shoes."],["Production concentration","Thailand and Indonesia account for approximately 80% of global natural rubber production (JPX)."]],"body":["RSS (ribbed smoked sheet) is made by coagulating latex, rolling it thinly, and then smoking and drying it. Conversely, blocks made by crushing, washing, drying, and compressing the coagulated material are TSR (technical standard rubber), and TSR20 is the most traded.","TSR20 is graded based on measured values ​​such as contamination, ash, nitrogen, volatile matter, and plastic retention index, so even for the same 20 grade, viscosity and processability differ depending on the production area and factory.","The tire industry is the largest consumer, and latex goes into gloves and medical supplies. Synthetic rubber prices and crude oil prices affect the demand for natural rubber."],"sources":[{"name":"JPX, Natural Rubber Futures(RSS3·TSR20) Factsheet","url":"https://www.jpx.co.jp/english/derivatives/products/rubber/RubberFuturesInformation/b5b4pj000003vdq6-att/Factsheet-Rubber_Futures_04122023_EN.pdf"}]},{"id":"fao-food-price-index","term":"FAO Food Price Index","ko":"FAO Food Price Index","cat":"agri","summary":"This is an index that looks at the monthly trend of international food raw material prices. Five product groups - grains, oils, meat, dairy products, and sugar - are weighted by their share of exports.","facts":[["as of","Calculated with the average price from 2014 to 2016 set to 100."],["Configuration","The average of the five indices of grains, vegetable oil, meat, dairy products, and sugar is weighted by the share of exports."],["Latest value","In October 2026, the grain price index was 116.8 and the overall food price index was 133.9 (FAO)."]],"body":["The FAO Food Price Index is indexed by converting the representative export price of each item into dollars. So, if the won exchange rate rises, domestic import costs may rise even if the index is the same.","The index is announced on a monthly basis, and the grain and oil index shows the direction of feed and food costs first. However, domestic consumer prices move differently from the index due to tariffs, distribution, and processing costs.","The FAO food price index and grain price index are included in the market chart on this page."],"sources":[{"name":"FAO, Food Price Index","url":"https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/foodpricesindex"}]},{"id":"lng-units","term":"LNG","ko":"LNG units and conversion","cat":"energy","summary":"It is a liquid made by cooling natural gas to -162°C. Its volume is reduced to 1/600, so it can be transported by ship, and the units of heat, weight, and volume are used together.","facts":[["Liquefaction","Cooling natural gas to -162°C reduces its volume by about 1/600."],["Calories","1 ton of LNG is approximately 52 MMBtu (51~54), and 1 million tons per year (1 Mtpa) is equivalent to approximately 1.36 bcm of natural gas."],["Unit","For international transactions, MMBtu, ton, and bcm are used together, and for Europe, it is expressed as MWh."]],"body":["LNG is made by removing impurities and cooling in a liquefaction plant. It is loaded into a tanker in liquid form, transported to the receiving base, then vaporized and sent to city gas pipes or power plants.","Contracts are usually based on thermal mass (MMBtu). Even if the tone is the same, the caloric content varies depending on the components, so mixing and comparing tones and MMBtu will result in errors.","Korea is an entirely importing country, and procures by adjusting the proportion of long-term contracts and spot (JKM). Winter demand and price differences between Europe and Asia affect domestic introduction prices."],"caution":"The calorific value of 1 ton of LNG ranges from 51 to 54 MMBtu, depending on the country of origin and ingredients. Calorie criteria (GCV) in the contract must be used for settlement.","sources":[{"name":"GIIGNL, LNG information","url":"https://giignl.org/"}]},{"id":"gas-benchmarks","term":"HH · TTF · JKM","ko":"Natural gas price index","cat":"energy","summary":"Natural gas uses different indicators depending on the region. Representative examples include American HH, European TTF, and Asian JKM, and their units are also different.","facts":[["US HH","Henry Hub is the standard US natural gas price expressed in USD/MMBtu."],["European TTF","Dutch TTF is traded in EUR/MWh and serves as the standard for European LNG introduction prices."],["Asia JKM","JKM is the Northeast Asian spot LNG valuation expressed in USD/MMBtu."]],"body":["The units of the three indicators are different, so conversion is required to compare them. 1 MMBtu is approximately 0.2931 MWh, and prices in Euros must be converted to dollars at the exchange rate.","In the US, HH remains low due to shale gas, and in Europe, TTF volatility has increased after the reduction of Russian pipeline gas. In Asia, freight charges apply to JKM, which increases the price difference with Europe.","LNG traders diversify cargo by looking at the arbitrage of the three markets. So a price surge in one region can pull up LNG supply and demand in other regions."],"sources":[{"name":"ICE, Dutch TTF Natural Gas Futures","url":"https://www.ice.com/products/27996665/Dutch-TTF-Natural-Gas-Futures"},{"name":"GIIGNL, LNG information","url":"https://giignl.org/"}]},{"id":"newcastle-coal","term":"NEWC Thermal Coal","ko":"Newcastle bituminous coal","cat":"energy","summary":"This is the Asian standard for high calorific power bituminous coal shipped from the Port of Newcastle, Australia. It is a different market from coking coal for steel.","facts":[["standard product","globalCOAL Newcastle standard product is 6,000 kcal/kg (NCV), ash less than 14%, and sulfur less than 0.75%."],["Price","The gC NEWC index is the benchmark for Asia-Pacific power coal prices, and ICE Newcastle futures are settled on this index."],["Distinguished from coking coal","Coking coal for steel (strong coal) goes to coke, and bituminous coal for power generation goes to fuel for thermal power generation."]],"body":["Bituminous coal is coal that is burned for power generation. Calorific value (kcal/kg), ash content, sulfur content, and moisture determine the price and environmental facility burden. The Newcastle standard is preferred in Asia due to its high calorific value and low sulfur content.","Coking coal has coking properties and must harden into coke at high temperatures, so its price is set separately. Even if they come from the same coal mine, different grades are traded in different markets.","The price of power generation coal is affected by demand from China and India, supply from Australia and Indonesia, and gas prices. When gas becomes more expensive, the share of coal-fired power generation increases and the price of coal may rise."],"sources":[{"name":"globalCOAL, SCoTA Specifications(NEWC)","url":"https://www.globalcoal.com/scota/specifications/"},{"name":"globalCOAL, NEWC Index Methodology","url":"https://www.globalcoal.com/coalprices/newcindexmethodology/"}]},{"id":"lithium-lce","term":"Lithium · LCE","ko":"Lithium and LCE conversion","cat":"energy","summary":"Lithium is traded as lithium carbonate, lithium hydroxide, and concentrated lithium, and lithium carbonate equivalent (LCE) is used when comparing contents.","facts":[["LCE conversion","1 ton of lithium is 5.323 tons of LCE, 1 ton of lithium hydroxide monohydrate is 0.880 tons of LCE, and 1 ton of lithium carbonate is 1.000 tons of LCE."],["Lithium carbonate composition","The lithium content of lithium carbonate (Li2CO3) is 18.8%."],["Ore","Spodumene concentrate is traded on a 6% Li2O(SC6) basis, with 1 tonne theoretically equivalent to 0.148 tonne LCE."]],"body":["There are many routes for lithium to be made from brine (brine) to lithium carbonate, from spodumene ore to lithium sulfate, and then to lithium hydroxide. Battery grade has a lower tolerance for impurities and is therefore more expensive than industrial grade.","Lithium hydroxide is mainly used in high-nickel NCM and NCA anode materials, and lithium carbonate is mainly used in LFP anode materials and glass and ceramics. Therefore, the price difference between the two products may widen.","Production from mines and brine projects is often reported in terms of lithium content (t Li), and chemical products are often reported in terms of LCE. Failure to match the units will result in incorrect comparisons of supplies."],"caution":"LCE is a stoichiometric conversion value. In actual transactions, the effective amount of lithium varies depending on grade, moisture, and recovery rate.","sources":[{"name":"British Geological Survey, Mineral profile: Lithium","url":"https://nora.nerc.ac.uk/id/eprint/534440/1/lithium_profile.pdf"},{"name":"USGS, Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — Lithium","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-lithium.pdf"}]},{"id":"cathode-material","term":"Cathode Material","ko":"Cathode materials NCM·NCA·LFP","cat":"energy","summary":"It is a material that determines the capacity of lithium-ion batteries. Nickel, cobalt, manganese series (NCM, NCA) and iron phosphate series (LFP) are the mainstream.","facts":[["NCM·NCA","It is a series of nickel, cobalt, manganese (or aluminum) oxides, and the higher the nickel proportion, the higher the energy density."],["LFP","It is a lithium, phosphate, and iron series and has good thermal stability and cost competitiveness, but its energy density is lower than NCM."],["Process","A precursor is made from metal sulfate, mixed with lithium compound and fired at high temperature to make a cathode material."]],"body":["Cathode materials account for a large portion of cell costs. Therefore, the prices of nickel, cobalt, and lithium directly affect cell costs, and manufacturers have changed their composition to reduce cobalt and increase nickel.","NCM is called 5:3:2, 6:2:2, 8:1:1, etc. depending on the nickel ratio. The more nickel there is, the longer the mileage is, but the more difficult it is to manage thermal stability and lifespan.","The proportion of LFP has increased in China and in entry-level electric vehicles and ESS. It is cheap and does not catch fire easily, but the energy stored for the same weight is small, so the vehicle weight and mileage design are different."],"sources":[{"name":"USGS, Lithium Use in Batteries(Circular 1371)","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/circ/1371/pdf/circ1371_508.pdf"},{"name":"USGS, Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — Lithium","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-lithium.pdf"}]},{"id":"anode-material","term":"Anode Material","ko":"Cathode material natural/artificial graphite","cat":"energy","summary":"It is a material that receives lithium ions when charging. It is made by spheroidizing and coating natural graphite or graphitizing needle coke.","facts":[["Natural graphite","Flake graphite is spheroidized and the surface is coated to use it as a cathode material. The USGS counts it separately as nodular graphite (SPG)."],["Artificial graphite","It is made by graphitizing petroleum needle coke at high temperature. It has better lifespan and charging characteristics than natural graphite, but its cost is high."],["Additives","Si cathode materials mixed with a small amount of silicon are also used to increase energy density.\nRetrieved from"]],"body":["Graphite is charged and discharged by inserting and removing lithium ions between the layer structures. Layer spacing and particle shape determine filling rate and lifetime.","Natural graphite is cheap, but requires nodularization and coating processes, and artificial graphite requires needle coke and graphitization power to increase the cost. Recently, natural and artificial materials have been mixed to match price and performance.","Because a high proportion of cathode materials are produced in China, diversifying the supply chain is considered a challenge. The United States and Europe are increasing their domestic production facilities."],"sources":[{"name":"USGS, Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — Graphite","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-graphite.pdf"}]},{"id":"cobalt","term":"Cobalt","ko":"Cobalt","cat":"energy","summary":"It is a strategic metal used in cathode materials and superalloys. It comes as a by-product of copper and nickel mining, and production is largely concentrated in the Democratic Republic of Congo.","facts":[["Production concentration","In 2025, the Democratic Republic of the Congo accounted for 73% of global cobalt mine production and Indonesia accounted for 14% (USGS)."],["LME Trading","The LME cobalt contract lot is 1 tonne."],["Purpose","It is used in lithium-ion battery cathode materials, superalloys, tool steels, and catalysts."]],"body":["A larger proportion of cobalt comes as a by-product of copper and nickel mines than from independent mines. Therefore, copper and nickel prices and Congo's policies determine cobalt supply.","In 2025, Congo temporarily banned exports and then switched to a quota system in response to oversupply and falling prices (USGS). When such a measure is announced, plans to procure battery and alloy raw materials are immediately shaken.","The battery industry has been developing low-cobalt and cobalt-free cathode materials that reduce the proportion of cobalt. Still, replacement is not easy in high-performance cathode materials and aviation superalloys."],"sources":[{"name":"USGS, Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — Cobalt","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-cobalt.pdf"}]},{"id":"gold","term":"Gold","ko":"Gold","cat":"energy","summary":"It is a precious metal with both investment and industrial demand. International prices are in dollars per troy ounce and wholesale units are 400 troy ounce bars.","facts":[["Unit","1 troy ounce is equal to 31.1035 grams."],["LBMA bar","The standard LBMA Good Delivery gold bar is approximately 400 troy ounces (12.5 kg)."],["Purpose","It is used as an investment, jewelry, electronics, dental, and industrial catalyst."]],"body":["Gold is chemically stable, does not corrode, and has good electrical conductivity, so it is used in electronic contacts and semiconductors. However, the main axis of demand is investment and accessories.","International prices are based on London LBMA prices and COMEX futures, and domestic prices are converted to won/gram and displayed with value-added tax and distribution costs added.","Gold tends to move in the opposite direction to the dollar and interest rates, and demand for safe assets increases when geopolitical risks increase. Therefore, we often react to interest rate and exchange rate news before real demand."],"sources":[{"name":"LBMA, Good Delivery","url":"https://www.lbma.org.uk/good-delivery"},{"name":"USGS, Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — Gold","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-gold.pdf"}]},{"id":"silver","term":"Silver","ko":"Silver","cat":"energy","summary":"It is the metal with the highest electrical conductivity and has both industrial and investment demand. Solar cells, electronics, and automobiles lead industrial demand.","facts":[["Industrial Demand","Silver industrial demand in 2024 was the highest ever at 680.5 million troy ounces (Silver Institute)."],["Solar power","In the same year, solar consumed 197.6 million troy ounces, accounting for 29% of industrial demand."],["Aggregate demand","In 2024, total silver demand exceeded supply at 1.1641 billion troy ounces, leading to a structural deficit."]],"body":["Silver has higher electrical conductivity than gold, so it is used in electronic components, solar cell electrodes, and automobile electronics. Industrial demand accounts for more than half of the total and is sensitive to economic and technological changes.","Although the amount of silver used per solar cell is decreasing due to technological advancements, the total demand has increased rapidly as the amount of installation has increased. Recently, high-efficiency cells such as TOPCon and HJT use more silver.","Silver prices are more volatile than gold, and industrial demand and investment demand move simultaneously, making it difficult to read the direction. In Korea, you need to look at the difference between the gold and silver price including VAT and the international price."],"sources":[{"name":"Silver Institute, World Silver Survey 2025","url":"https://www.silverinstitute.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/World_Silver_Survey-2025.pdf"},{"name":"Silver Institute announces silver industry demand in 2024","url":"https://silverinstitute.org/silver-industrial-demand-reached-a-record-680-5-moz-in-2024/"}]},{"id":"pgm","term":"Platinum · Palladium","ko":"Platinum and palladium","cat":"energy","summary":"It is a key precious metal in automobile exhaust gas catalyst. Gasoline cars mainly use palladium, diesel cars mainly use platinum, and a large proportion of them are produced in South Africa and Russia.","facts":[["Main use","Platinum, palladium, and rhodium are used in automobile catalysts (catalytic converters) to purify exhaust gas."],["Production","Platinum is largely produced in South Africa, and palladium is largely produced in Russia and South Africa. South African PGM production in 2025 will be 9% lower than the previous year (USGS)."],["Replaced","Palladium has replaced platinum in gasoline catalysts, and diesel catalysts can contain up to 25% palladium."]],"body":["Catalytic converters change carbon monoxide, nitrogen oxides, and hydrocarbons in exhaust gases into harmless substances. This reaction requires platinum, palladium, and rhodium, several grams per car.","The spread of electric vehicles reduces the demand for automobile catalysts, but hydrogen fuel cells and chemical catalysts support platinum demand. So, platinum must look at the three markets together: automobile, hydrogen, and chemical.","Precious metals are recovered from spent catalysts. Increasing recycling volumes will ease the supply shock even if mine production declines."],"sources":[{"name":"USGS, Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — Platinum-group metals","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-platinum-group.pdf"}]},{"id":"pulp","term":"NBSK · BHKP","ko":"Pulp grade","cat":"energy","summary":"It is wood pulp, the raw material for paper. It is divided into softwood long fiber (NBSK) and broadleaf short fiber (BHKP), and has different strength and surface properties.","facts":[["fiber length","Softwood fibers are on average three times longer than hardwood fibers, which increases the strength of the paper."],["NBSK","This is bleached kraft pulp made from softwood in North America and is the standard for market pulp prices."],["BHKP","Bleached hardwood kraft pulp mixed with printing, writing paper, tissue, and cardboard to smooth the surface."]],"body":["The Kraft method boils wood chips in an alkaline solution to dissolve the lignin and separate the fibers. It is then bleached into white pulp, which is then dissolved in water and made into paper at a paper mill.","Softwood pulp is mainly used for packaging materials and industrial papers that require strength, and hardwood pulp is mainly used for products that require printability and softness. So, paper manufacturers mix the two pulps to achieve the desired physical properties.","Pulp is produced in Canada, Northern Europe, South America, and Indonesia and traded at international prices. Log prices, energy costs, freight rates, and Chinese demand drive prices."],"sources":[{"name":"CEPI, Definitions and Concepts(2025)","url":"https://www.cepi.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/2025-CEPI-Definitions-and-Concepts.pdf"},{"name":"USITC, Wood Pulp and Waste Paper","url":"https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub3490.pdf"}]}]};
